PATCH 260: the per-frame subtask DISPATCH loop FUN_1000_b040 -- record-cursor + CS-relative
method-table base-loss (SIGSEGV), reached from the 461b frame rotator (patch 259) via the background
task b02a.

b02a (0x1b02a) decrements a cooldown DAT_2000_5ce5 and, when it expires, calls b040 with bx=0x9dc7 (a
DGROUP near offset).  b040 (asm 0x1b040) walks 16 subtask records at DGROUP:0x9dc7 (stride 0xe) and for
each NEAR-calls `[CS:(word[bx]-0x4637)]` (CS=0x1000).  Ghidra base-lost the record cursor (param_1 =
&DAT_2000_5dc7 host ptr, int stride 7=28B vs the asm 0xe=14B) AND the CS-relative jump-table read
(rendered `*(undefined2*)(si-0x4637)` -> host deref of a tiny address -> SIGSEGV).  Rebuilt faithfully
in the DGROUP/CS model; the method-offset table is at CS=0x1000 (the dispatched subtasks 0xb059/0xb062/
... sit immediately after b040 in the seg-0x1000 region).  The asm testb [0x6dab],0 guard is dead
(always false) and elided.  Mission-cascade only.
